       <narrative xml:lang="EN">The indicator will support the country&apos;s response to health-related emergencies, particularly through the development, adoption and dissemination of 22 case management guidelines and procedures for national priority diseases. Progress is tracked through the number of health workers trained on clinical case management guidelines and procedures for national priority diseases. To avoid double-counting, a methodology that counts the health workers, not the instances of training, will be developed.</narrative>
